desktop-shell: Bluetooth icon on the taskbar

A Bluetooth icon left of the volume, shown only when the computer has a
Bluetooth adapter. It is dimmed while Bluetooth is off and has a cyan dot
while a device is connected; the tooltip names the connected device.

A click opens a menu: turn Bluetooth on or off, the paired devices (a
click connects or disconnects one) and "Bluetooth settings" (Settings,
on its Bluetooth page; "Add a device..." when nothing is paired yet).

The state comes from "hexa-bluetooth status", read in the background
every few seconds like the volume, and again soon after a change.

